55,3,1,talk,Victoria,,Option A is the cheapest and most stable. I vote for Fixed Desks.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Minato,,Option A lets me keep my ergonomic settings and pick a quiet spot. I vote A.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,May,,Option C is a nightmare for my schedule. Option B is too much shuffling. I vote A.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option A creates a permanent class of ""window"" and ""wall"" people. I prefer Option B for fairness.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Option C sounds social, but Option A with a good layout could work. I'll vote B to ensure we mix.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, we can just rotate the assignments manually every year if needed.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, rotating blocks sounds like it would ruin my workstation setup every few months.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, rotating blocks still sounds like a lot of ""half-packed boxes"" and interruptions.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, manual rotation is just a delayed version of Option B. I still prefer B.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, I see your point. Maybe stability is more important for the team's focus.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Victoria,,Let's stick to the most efficient path. A is the only one that doesn't waste time or money.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Minato,,I agree. Stability is comfort.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,May,,"I'm staying with A. No morning setup, no chaos.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,I can't bring myself to vote for a permanent hierarchy of seats. I'm staying with B.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I'll change my vote to A. The productivity loss of shuffling seems too high.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
